The affects folder contains affectsStore.ts, a module-level cache of the last known active-affects list. It mirrors the existing features/room/roomDataStore.ts pattern: useAffectsBlock.ts seeds its initial state from this cache and writes every update back to it, so remounting the hook (as happens when the HUD theme's shell swaps live) shows the last-known affects immediately instead of flashing empty. useSanctuaryActive.ts deliberately reuses this same cache rather than keeping its own, since sanctuary presence is just a derived boolean over the same underlying affects data.
